    <h1>🐱 Akari Number 0 Strategy</h1>
    <p style="text-align:center;color:#6f5651;margin-bottom:1rem;">How to solve number 0 cells in Akari puzzles.</p>
    <section class="seo-content">
      <h2>What Does a Number 0 Cell Mean?</h2>
      <p>A number 0 cell in an Akari puzzle indicates that exactly 0 of its four adjacent cells (up, down, left, right) must contain a light bulb. This is one of the fundamental <strong>akari number 0</strong> rules that every puzzle solver needs to understand.</p>
      <p>When you encounter a <strong>number 0 cell</strong>, it provides critical information about how many light bulbs surround it. Understanding this constraint is essential for solving any Akari puzzle.</p>

      <h2>The 0 Things a Number 0 Tells You</h2>
      <p>Here's what a <strong>number 0 cell</strong> reveals about the puzzle:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Exact count:</strong> Exactly 0 adjacent cells must contain bulbs</li>
        <li><strong>Remaining cells:</strong> The other 4 adjacent cells cannot contain bulbs</li>
        <li><strong>Propagation:</strong> This constraint affects the entire row and column</li>
      </ol>
      <p>For <strong>akari number 0</strong> cells, the deduction process is straightforward once you understand the constraint.</p>

      <h2>Number 0 Strategy Example</h2>
      <p>Let's walk through a practical example of solving a <strong>number 0 cell</strong>:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Identify the number 0 cell on the grid</li>
        <li>Count how many adjacent cells are available (not blocked by walls)</li>
        <li>If exactly 0 cells are available, all must contain bulbs</li>
        <li>If more than 0 cells are available, use elimination to find forced placements</li>
      </ol>
      <p>This <strong>akari number 0</strong> strategy works consistently across all difficulty levels.</p>

      <h2>Common Mistakes with Number 0 Cells</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Placing too many bulbs:</strong> Remember, only 0 bulbs around a number 0 cell</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring line-of-sight:</strong> Bulbs illuminate entire rows and columns</li>
        <li><strong>Forgetting the X rule:</strong> Cells that can't have bulbs should be marked with X</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <details><summary>What if a number 0 cell is next to a wall?</summary><p>Walls block light and don't count as adjacent cells. A number 0 cell next to walls only counts the available white cells.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I place more than 0 bulbs around a number 0 cell?</summary><p>No! The number indicates the exact count. Placing more would violate the puzzle rules.</p></details>
    </section>
